  "html": "<p>Mythic Items are also known as Rainbow Items, named due to their rainbow-colored titles. These items are on the highest tier of loot ranking, that can be worn or wielded. These items are <a href=\"/wiki/Soulbound\" title=\"Soulbound\">soulbound</a> within 10 minutes, but are soulbound immediately when purchased from a vendor using <a href=\"/wiki/Kings_Coins\" title=\"Kings Coins\">King's Coins</a>. \n</p><p>Only 5% of mythic items dropped by mobs can be used by non-members. \n</p><p>Drop odds are on <a href=\"/wiki/Rainbow_Drops\" title=\"Rainbow Drops\">Rainbow Drops</a>. Named lair-chest pieces are on <a href=\"/wiki/Boss_Lair_Rainbows\" title=\"Boss Lair Rainbows\">Boss Lair Rainbows</a>. Shared-pool level bands are on <a href=\"/wiki/Rainbow_Level_Bands\" title=\"Rainbow Level Bands\">Rainbow Level Bands</a>. Well-only names are on <a href=\"/wiki/Well-Only_Rainbows\" title=\"Well-Only Rainbows\">Well-Only Rainbows</a>. Names that no longer drop are on <a href=\"/wiki/Discontinued_Rainbows\" title=\"Discontinued Rainbows\">Discontinued Rainbows</a>.</p>\n<p>Below is a listing of all mythic (or rainbow) items.\n</p><p>NOTE: Fighter Rainbow Armor, Ranger Rainbow Armor and Mage Rainbow Armor categories will show all armor one can equip. The Rainbow Body armor will show all bodies for all classes.\n</p>\n<p>A lot of later rainbows work that way: fixed name and look, a joke ending for the primaries, and unnamed rolls for the rest. Named pieces can also have baked bonuses that every copy shares. The item pages say which rolls that piece actually has.</p>\n\n<div id=\"mw-subcategories\">\n<h2>Subcategories</h2>\n<p>There are 18 subcategories to this category.\n</p><table width=\"100%\"><tr valign=\"top\"><td>\n<h3>F</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Category/Fighter_Rainbow_Armor\" title=\"Category:Fighter Rainbow Armor\">Fighter Rainbow Armor</a></li></ul>\n<h3>G</h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Category/Growth_Items\" title=\"Category:Growth Items\">Growth It